---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_DATA } from '../constants';
import portraitImage from '../assets/portrait.png';

import '../styles/about.css';
---

<Layout pageTitle="About">
    <div class="page-container">
        <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

        <div class="about-content">
 
            <section>
                <ul class="custom-list">
                   <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Do you provide worksheets or study guides?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Yes. I've accumulated a vast array of textbooks and problem sets. I'll often provide my students with problem sets so they can continue building their skills after our session is over. I also frequently make electronic flash cards for students who are studying a memorization-intensive course.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">How long is an average session?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">An hour and a half is a typical session length. I ask that sessions be a minimum of an hour long.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Do you assign homework?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Yes, if it is needed.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Can I share my session with another student?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Sure! Ask me about my special rates for group sessions.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Do you tutor in person on online?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">I do much of my tutoring on Zoom. I'm located in NYC, so I'm available to in-person sessions.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">What happens if I have to cancel? Do I still have to pay for the session?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">I require 24 hours of notice for cancellations, or I will expect you to pay for the session you missed.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">What forms of payment do you accept?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Cash, Venmo, PayPal, and Zelle.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Do you offer any referral bonuses?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Yes. If you recommend me to another student, and that student hires me for four hours or more, you get one hour of free tutoring.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">What is a typical session like for high school and college tutoring on academic subjects?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">For academic subjects, my students are usually already enrolled in a course in high school or college. Usually we go over homework together, I teach them new information as it is needed to answer the questions, and try to guide them through their homework without directly answering the question for them. This helps my students increase their problem solving ability. I can also lecture if needed, make up problems for practice, and assign problems additional practice on their own time. Oftentimes I will create reference sheets for my students as I tutor them, and sometimes I have reference sheets already prepared. Usually we'll meet for an hour and a half.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">What is a typical session like for test prep?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Test prep tutoring is different, because usually it is not in conjunction with another class, so I'll spend more time lecturing and explaining concepts, and then we'll go over problems together, and I'll assign homework that we can go over at the next session.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">How can you be contacted?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">HIOAHOIHIOHOOIH</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
